Notes on Recode File


1.   The 230 clusters were numbered from 1 to 222 and from 261 to 411 (in the
     following sequence: 261 291 321 371 381 391 401 411) due to a subdivision of
     E.A. in the capital where the population increased a lot since the last
     census. The sequences of those new numbers have a correspondence with the
     cluster number they were extracted from. For example, cluster 261 is a
     subdivision or a part of the previous cluster 26. For HV001, the cluster
     numbering is the same as in the raw data, and for HV004 it is sequential up
     to 230.

2.   The education level presents a common particularity of many african french
     speaking countries.  The secondary level is divided into the first and second
     stages of secondary education. The first stage is four years and the second
     one is 3 years. There are country specific variables to keep track of theses
     two stages. However, they were recoded as in the standard in one stage
     secondary education adding the number of years of the second stage to the
     number of years of the first one.

3.   A total of 6 years at primary, 5 and 4 years at first and second stages of
     secondary level and 4 years at higher are necessary to complete those
     education levels. However, a maximum of 7 years was assigned to complete
     secondary level instead of nine years (5 + 4), because of the professional
     training they added at the end of the two stages secondary level which is
     optional.

4.   The distribution of the respondentþs month of birth the distribution after
     imputation is low for January. Itþs partly due to fact that during imputation
     the year of birth reported was ignored assuming that people know their age
     better than their date of birth (date of birth is month and year of birth)
     and/or because the interviewers were inclined to subtract the year of birth
     from the year of interview to report the age.

5.   There are 222 women who know Norplant and only 17 of them declared  having
     ever used it. Norplant was recoded in the raw data as a new category only in
     section SEC31 and in variable Q329 to show the impact of a recent campaign
     at the time of the survey. In the raw data there are 227 yes for the
     knowledge but five of them are not Norplant (the difference comes from the
     way the other answer can be recoded in SEC31) and 18 cases for the use with
     the occurrence 13 (second 12 of the other answers) because one case had ever
     used another traditional method which is the second traditional method ever
     used: the occurrence is 13 but Q301(13)=12.

6.   The recodification for variables M1-M32 can be slightly different from the
     raw data in their distribution, due to the standard recode process of
     breastfeeding, abstinence and amenorrhea. For example there are two cases
     more in the raw data that are respectively 19 and 36 months of duration of
     breastfeeding and they are missing in the recode data because of the way the
     recode recalculate durations and recategorize special answers with others raw
     variables.

7.   Variable V416 is created from questions Q471, Q475, Q483, Q484, and variable
     V208.  Variables V424A-X were created from Q488 and V416 (equal 2 or 3). It
     was not possible to use question Q471A (V416 = 1) to create V424A because the
     categories are different; so these questions were kept as country specific
     variables (S471A-H).

8.   Vaccination questions (Q444 and Q447) are recoded into standard recode
     variables (H2-H9) and into country specific variables (S444 and S447) to keep
     track of immovax which is a country specific vaccination. Two immovax shots
     are equal to 3 Polio and 3 DPT injections.  When the mother reported more
     than 3 shots, it is assumed that these extra shots (only two for immovax)
     were for measles first and then yellow fever.

9.   The distribution for the respondentþs month of marriage is unusual, as is the
     case with the month of birth.  The month of marriage was imputed considering
     the age at first marriage (if reported), and so the year was ignored assuming
     that people better know their age at marriage than their date of marriage,
     and also to adjust the fact that the interviewers were inclined to subtract
     the year of marriage from the year of interview to report the age.

10.  The labels PSP and CSPS are not translated because there is no equivalent in
     English. Meanwhile, the label SMI (Sant‚ Maternel et Infantile) is translated
     into MCH center (Maternal and Children Health center)


Inconsistencies in the Data File

1.   There are 2 cases in which the number of single years of education is close
     to the age of the respondent (respectively V133 and V012). It is probably
     that those respondents have skipped some grades.

2.   There is one woman who takes pills and at the same time, her husband has been
     sterilized

3.   There are two missing answers for the brand pills and their costs.

4.   There are two cases where V426=NOTAPPL and M4=0.  Both are dead children
     breastfeed.

5.   Two children got vaccination card without any vaccination dates on it.

6.   Three cases in which the respondent declared not knowing if they had given
     any treatment for diarrhea H21A=8 and they did not give anything
     (H13=NOTAPPL, H14=0 H15-H15H=NOTAPPL) .

7.   Twelve cases are inconsistent between the height the weight and the result
     of the measurement (either one of the measure is 0 or missing and the result
     is 0 or the result is not zero and the two measures are written down).

8.   There is one woman married, living with her husband, she is his only wife,
     and she never had sex at the time of interview, but she is only sixteen years
     old.

9.   Twenty-one respondents answered that they had their first intercourse more
     than one year later than their first birth.

10.  About 48 responses are inconsistent between time since last sex and whether
     they had sex in the last four weeks or since last birth.

11.  There are three MISSING responses for the time for future birth. In fact part
     of the response is given (if it is in months or years), but the number of
     months or years is missing.

12.  Seven women are currently working, but their occupation is "no occupation."
     It is probably due to the confusion between working and having a job.

13.  One case is of a respondent working away but her occupation is missing:
     V718=MISSING and V721=2.


