Notes on Male Recode File


1.   The recode file for the men is based on a DHSIII structure. That is why
     we have þBF3" instead of þBF2" in the variable MV000, unlike in the
     variable HV000 where þBF2"was coded, because the womenþs recode file is
     based on a DHSII structure.
     There are many others variables that are in the menþs, but not in the
     womenþs recode file, because of this structure difference.

2.   Like the women, the 230 clusters numbered from 1 to 222 and from 261 to
     411 in the survey, in the following sequence: 261 291 321 371 381 391
     401 411 (in the capital where the population increased a lot since the
     last census the E.A.s 26 , 29, 32, 37, 38, 39, 40, 41 where subdivised
     in two).For MV001, the cluster numbering is the same as in the raw data,
     and for MV004 it is sequential up to 230.

3.   In the education level, the secondary level is divided into the first
     and second stage of secondary education. The first stage is four years
     and the second one is 3 years. There are country specific recoded
     variables (SM105 and SM 106) to keep track of theses two stages.
     However, they were recoded as in the standart in one stage secondary
     education adding the number of years of the second stage to the number
     of years of the first one.

4.   A total of 6 years at primary, 5 and 4 years at first and second stage
     of secondary level and 4 years at higher are necessary to complete those
     education level. However, the maximun put down in the recode application
     is 7 years for the whole secondary level, instead of nine years (5 + 4),
     because of the professional training they added at the end of the two
     stages secondary level which is optional.

5.   For the respondentþs month of birth the distribution after imputation is low
     for January.
     Itþs partly due to fact that during imputation the year of birth reported was
     ignored assuming that people better know their age than their date of birth
     (date of birth is month and year of birth) and/or the interviewers were
     inclined to substract the year of birth from the year of interview to report
     the age.

6.   Three men were (supposed to be) born the last century. Their year and month
     of birth (date of birth) were recoded in the category þ-1: Last centuryþ and
     their age was recode þ97: 97 and olderþ.

7.   The duration of interview is negative in twenty cases, and over than one
     hour and a half in twelve cases.  There are few cases (two exactly)
     where the duration was approximately about twelve hours and twenty
     minutes, due to a confusion writing times in the format 1-12 am or pm
     instead of 1-24 hours. For those two men, (cluster=31 household=1 line=1
     and cluster=54 household=2 line=2), if the duration was positive, and
     the ending interview time equal or over than 10pm, with the starting
     interview time a bit more than 12 hours before (for cluster=31
     household=1 line=1 starting time=10:15 ending time=22:34), twelve hours
     are substracted to the ending time in the recode, or added to the
     starting time of interview when the ending time is less than 10pm (after
     recode cluster=31 household=1 line=1 starting time=10:15 ending
     time=10:34) . If the duration was negative, (for cluster=54 household=2
     line=1 starting time=19:25 ending time=7:38), and the starting time
     equal or over 10pm, with th ending time a bit more than 12 hours before,
     twelve hours are substracted to the starting time in the recode, or if
     the starting time is less than 10pm, twelve hours are added to the
     ending time of interview (after recode cluster=54 household=2 line=1
     starting time=19:25 ending time=19:38).

8.   There is no information about the husband line number in the female
     questionnaire, but you can find it in the household schedules. So the husband
     line number, was taken from the household data (M17), and recoded in a
     country specific variable (SH17). The information was checked at the men and
     women level matching the consistencies with other informations (checking the
     marital status and in the menþs cases the wives line number) during the male
     recoding process.

9.   The variables MV763, MV764 and MV765 about number of partners and knowledge
     and use of condom concern the population who had sex only the last two
     months. In the questionnaire, only people who had sex the last two months
     where interviewed about their use of condom and the number of their sexual
     partners. However, the question M415 was recoded as well in a country
     specific variables (SM415A-E) to keep track of informations about Aids and
     STDs separatly.
Inconsistencies in the Male Data File


1.   There are 53 cases where the current marital status is different between
     the household data and the male data (HV115<>MV501), and whithin thoses
     53 cases, 44 of them with a difference between the past and present
     marital status (HV116<>MV502). This is probably due to different
     respondant and sometimes confusion in the definition of being married
     (people who live together are often used to say that they are husband
     and wife).

2.   There are 3 cases where the wifeþs age is below fifteen, that make the
     wives not eligible. These three household are the household=5 in
     cluster=24, the household=14 in cluster=140, and the household=12 int
     cluster=177.

3.   In 33 cases the duration of interview is negative or over one hour and
     a half. Two cases were corrected as described above, eleven were put in
     the categorie of 95 minutes and over, and the twenty other cases were
     recoded inconsistent (97).

4.   Cluster=21 household=5 line=1, the man declare using a contraception
     that is periodic abstinence and he declared not ever having used any.
     (MV312=8 MV302=0 MV305=5).

5.   Two men sterilized answered that they expected time for a future birth
     soon or in few month. They could sterilized after the start of the last
     pregnancy. Those two men are: cluster=123 household=21 line=1 and
     cluster=261 household=37 line=3.

